      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 5.64,
          "en": "So how does this Riverpod package work then?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.64,
          "end": 7.29,
          "en": "Well, in your Flutter app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.29,
          "end": 9.84,
          "en": "with that Riverpod package installed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.84,
          "end": 12.48,
          "en": "you can create a so-called provider,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.48,
          "end": 15.21,
          "en": "which is some kind of object created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.21,
          "end": 18.513,
          "en": "based on a class that is provided by the Riverpod package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.5,
          "end": 21.81,
          "en": "Now, this provider then can provide",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.81,
          "end": 23.94,
          "en": "a potentially dynamic value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.94,
          "end": 26.07,
          "en": "and it can also provide methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.07,
          "end": 29.1,
          "en": "that may change that value in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.1,
          "end": 32.52,
          "en": "And then in your application, in any of your widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.52,
          "end": 35.67,
          "en": "not just your screen widgets, but any widgets,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 35.67,
          "end": 38.82,
          "en": "you can set up a consumer that is connected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.82,
          "end": 41.64,
          "en": "to the provider and it will be connected automatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 41.64,
          "end": 43.11,
          "en": "by the Riverpod package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.11,
          "end": 45.09,
          "en": "And in that consumer widget,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.09,
          "end": 48.87,
          "en": "you can then listen to changes to that provider value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.87,
          "end": 52.65,
          "en": "or even trigger those changes by calling those methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.65,
          "end": 55.8,
          "en": "that might be provided by the provider.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.8,
          "end": 57.03,
          "en": "That's how it works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.03,
          "end": 59.79,
          "en": "And because you have this central provider",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 59.79,
          "end": 62.46,
          "en": "and any widget can set up a consumer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 62.46,
          "end": 66.42,
          "en": "you don't need to pass these cross-state management values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.42,
          "end": 68.01,
          "en": "between those widgets anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 68.01,
          "end": 72.03,
          "en": "Instead, every widget can directly connect to the provider,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.03,
          "end": 74.19,
          "en": "and that's what we're now going to implement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 74.19,
          "end": 76.05,
          "en": "First with a basic example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 76.05,
          "end": 79.023,
          "en": "and then step-by-step with more complex examples.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
